WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
أعوذ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
(36:1) يسٓ

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
(36:2) وَٱلْقُرْءَانِ ٱلْحَكِيمِ

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
(36:3) إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
(36:4) عَلَىٰ صِرَٰطٍ مُّسْتَقِيمٍ

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:42.000
(36:5) تَنزِيلَ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.000
(36:6) لِتُنذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّآ أُنذِرَ ءَابَآؤُهُمْ فَهُمْ غَـٰفِلُونَ

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:02.000
(36:7) لَقَدْ حَقَّ ٱلْقَوْلُ عَلَىٰٓ أَكْثَرِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:18.000
(36:8) إِنَّا جَعَلْنَا فِىٓ أَعْنَـٰقِهِمْ أَغْلَـٰلًا فَهِىَ إِلَى ٱلْأَذْقَانِ فَهُم مُّقْمَحُونَ

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:37.000
وَجَعَلْنَا مِنۢ بَيْنِ أَيْدِيهِمْ سَدًّا وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ سَدًّا فَأَغْشَيْنَـٰهُمْ فَهُمْ (36:9) لَا يُبْصِرُونَ

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:51.000
(36:10) وَسَوَآءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ ءَأَنذَرْتَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تُنذِرْهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:10.000
إِنَّمَا تُنذِرُ مَنِ ٱتَّبَعَ ٱلذِّكْرَ وَخَشِىَ ٱلرَّحْمَـٰنَ بِٱلْغَيْبِ ۖ فَبَشِّرْهُ (36:11) بِمَغْفِرَةٍ وَأَجْرٍ كَرِيمٍ

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:32.000
إِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْىِ ٱلْمَوْتَىٰ وَنَكْتُبُ مَا قَدَّمُوا۟ وَءَاثَـٰرَهُمْ ۚ وَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ (36:12) أَحْصَيْنَـٰهُ فِىٓ إِمَامٍ مُّبِينٍ

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:53.000
But that night, in April, I opened Quran as usual and read the place where usually... the top right. And it said you're going to hell.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:00.000
So, I closed it again and said this is Satan telling me, trying to fighting me with giving me bad time. So, I said

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.000
أعوذ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:10.000
And please God protect me from Satan. I seek refuge in You. And I said it in many different ways

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:22.000
and then I opened it again at random as usual and it said you're fired. You will not do the job. You're a chicken. You're not suitable. And you are going to hell.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:31.000
So, I sought refuge in God again from Satan, from the devil in stronger terms for a longer time. I made SUJUD

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:38.000
Then, I opened the Quran again at random. It said you're fired. You're going to hell. You're doomed. You're not gonna do it. We'll find somebody else to do the job.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.000
So, I closed it again. It is now defying statistics or coincidence.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:55.000
So, I turned to God very hard and I said please, God, let me know if this is coincidence or why is it giving me these bad ideas.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:06.000
So, I opened and I kept doing this and repeatedly every time, I opened. It said you're fired. You're no good. You're going to hell. You're doomed.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:15.000
And it was getting worse. Until I reached the conviction, a real conviction in my heart, that I'm doomed. I'm going to hell.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Then, I started to cry. And I started to repent. And I opened it and as if the Quran had nothing in it except you're fired. You're going to hell.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:38.000
You're not gonna do the work. We'll substitute somebody in your place. So, I said this Quran is rigged. Maybe, because I'm using it a lot.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:50.000
So, I got this one which was brand new. And I opened it. It said you're fired. You're going to hell. You cannot do the job. You're a chicken. We'll substitute somebody in your place.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:59.000
So, I closed it again and I opened another place. The Quran had nothing in it except... I got the English Quran and I opened it.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:08.000
I looked in a neutral spot. You're fired. You'll not do the job. You're going to hell. So, it is no longer coincidence.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.000
I got this big book, this big Quran, here.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:20.000
And I opened it this way. I mean, I did all kinds of crazy things to let the Quran open at random and go like this.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:29.000
And then I opened the Quran and looked in it. And it say you're going to hell. You're doomed. You cannot do the job. You're fired.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:37.000
So, with this, I got... Oh, I got a letter opener and I stacked the Qurans

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
like this and I point. I closed my eyes and pointed the letter opener

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
and inserted it in one of these pages and opened it

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:58.000
and it tell me the same thing. There was nothing in the Quran that morning except you're fired. You cannot do the job. Get out of here. You're doomed. I don't need you anymore. I substitute somebody else in your place.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:11.000
So, I cried and I made SUJUD. And I repented. I sought refuge from Satan and it kept giving me the same message.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:19.000
So, I became convinced that God is speaking to me through the Quran and I became convinced that I'm no good,

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:25.000
that I'm fired, that I'm going to hell. And I cried as hard as I never did in my life.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:31.000
I really became convinced that I'm finished and I'm doomed and there is no salvation inside.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:38.000
I... my SUJUD became longer, my crying was harder. There was nobody in the mosque.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:51.000
And then one time, I opened the Quran and it said We forgive you. Oh, I reached the conviction with all this crying that...

00:06:51.000 --> 00:07:05.000
now, the message was very clear that I am not coming out with an announcement that I am God's messenger.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:17.000
I have known it since 1980 and I ignored messages that say... there are verses in Quran that say say O, people I'm God's messenger to all of you.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:24.000
And I ignored those. They were very loud and very clear and I ignored them. Obviously, the timing was not right, then. I mean, now in retrospect

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:38.000
I was supposed to have ignored those messages. They got loud and repeated and louder and clearer and I kept ignoring them until this happened. So, there is something that led to this.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:44.000
I mean, I opened the Quran says say O, people I'm God's messenger for all of you.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:57.000
And I became convinced that this is no longer the case. Then, with these repetitions, I reached the decision... in my repentance,

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:11.000
I said please God accept my repentance. Take me back even if I lose my own children, my friends, if I lose everybody, I will, I will do anything. I will go out and I will make the announcement.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:21.000
And I really had that conviction cause I said chances are my children will tell me get out of here. You're a crazy man. What are you talking about?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:34.000
So, it became my neck. And there are verses in Quran where it says the person disowns his own parents, his own children. The children disown their parents and so on. It became a reality for me.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:47.000
And here I am doomed, going to hell. And all things are hinging on courage. God doesn’t want a coward to work for him.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.000
It became very obvious.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:09:00.000
So, when I really reached the conviction that I will do it at any expense, I got this message that said you're forgiven. We'll accept your repentance.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:06.000
And my crying of sadness became crying of joy.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.000
And I still didn’t believe that remark. Maybe, it's a fluke.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:21.000
So, I did the same thing and there was nothing in the Quran except We accept your repentance. You're forgiven. Go now and do the job. God is Forgiver, Merciful.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:27.000
And I did it in the same way. I mean, this defied all statistic and all coincidence.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.000
The background to this...

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:44.000
This is why I'm not... people who around me know that I'm not making any bones about it. I'm not being humble about it and I could not take any chances.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:56.000
And I believe if it happens again, I will be really fired and be sent to Hell. And I'm not gonna do it. So, this is why I have been bold.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:010:08.000
And it really has nothing to do with humbleness or modesty. If we understand a few basic things in the Quran. One thing is that a messenger is no big deal.

00:010:08.000 --> 00:010:16.000
That it is a big deal only if we idolize the messengers. We get the picture in our mind...

00:010:16.000 --> 00:010:20.000
...and this is the typical response with all the believers.

00:010:21.000 --> 00:010:30.000
The people who were averse from the beginning, they just continued to be averse or maybe a little bit worse.

00:010:30.000 --> 00:010:40.000
Except their harsh attacks had a little bit of reverence in, as if in the background, it said what if he is?

00:010:41.000 --> 00:010:50.000
I get this telephone calls on the machine and in the past, they used to call me bad names and all that but

00:010:50.000 --> 00:010:58.000
now they say... they read Quran. And they read the verses that says fear God.

00:010:58.000 --> 00:011:05.000
And then they add come back to Islam. This kind of thing. But you can sense the kind of respect they have at the back of their mind.

00:011:07.000 --> 00:011:11.000
This is the difference that happened with the opponents.

00:011:11.000 --> 00:011:20.000
And this is because of their reverence for RASOOL ALLAH. This word, they made it so big and put it next to God.

00:011:20.000 --> 00:011:26.000
And this is why it's a big deal for them. But if we understand the Quran, we'll find out that it is not a big deal

00:011:26.000 --> 00:011:38.000
because the Quran teaches us that a messenger is not necessarily better than anyone in the world, in the generation, or anyone around him.

00:011:39.000 --> 00:011:55.000
We have this lesson in SURA 18 where Moses, one of the big messengers of God met someone who's described as one of God's servants. one of Our servants God says.

00:011:55.000 --> 00:012:05.000
And this one of God's servants began teaching Moses a few lessons and Moses turned out to be a lousy student.

00:012:05.000 --> 00:012:16.000
So, this is teaching us that the messenger, the biggest ones, are not any better than anyone around them. I mean, not necessarily better than people around them.

00:012:17.000 --> 00:012:27.000
The Quran teaches that say I'm a human being like you. And this is about the prophet Muhammad, for example.

00:012:27.000 --> 00:012:40.000
The Quran teaches that the criterion for closeness to God is righteousness, not being a messenger or not being the most knowledgeable or the richest or the tallest

00:012:40.000 --> 00:012:49.000
or anything else. Righteousness. Nothing else. So, and anyone can be more righteous than the messenger or anybody else.

00:012:51.000 --> 00:012:58.000
There is also a verse in SURA 39 that says that being a messenger of God does not even guarantee Heaven. It is no guarantee.

00:012:59.000 --> 00:013:15.000
It says. I'm quoting the Quran, now. It says that's what We revealed to you and to those before you that if you ever fall in idol worship, in idolatry, all your work will be nullified and you'll be a loser.

00:013:17.000 --> 00:013:28.000
So, if people understand this, they won't make a big deal out of being a messenger of God. I called Atef and I told him about this.

00:013:28.000 --> 00:013:37.000
and he... logically, he started to discuss the wisdom of making an announcement like this and why is it necessary.

00:013:38.000 --> 00:013:49.000
And I found myself him and I talking as if I sat down and decided to make an announcement. Then, it dawned on me it's not really my decision. It was not my decision at all.

00:013:49.000 --> 00:013:55.000
Obviously, God wants this announcement to be made for reasons that only God knows.

00:013:55.000 --> 00:013:57.000
And we can speculate on.

00:013:58.000 --> 00:014:08.000
The first verse in SURA 67 says God created death and life to test us, to test the people.

00:014:09.000 --> 00:014:18.000
Cause before that there was no death. Before the human race came here, there was no death. This is why God says He created death.

00:014:18.000 --> 00:014:19.000
mentioned death before life.

00:014:19.000 --> 00:014:33.000
The whole purpose is a test. And it turns out and we know now that the road to God is full of traps on the side for people to fall off. They drop out.

00:014:33.000 --> 00:014:46.000
And when you hear somebody say I'm a messenger of God. Some people drop out. And it's part of the sifting process. There are so many traps along the road.

00:014:46.000 --> 00:014:57.000
And the matter is decided, really, from the very beginning. I mean, a person who has doubts, who is not a sincere believer will fall off at one of these traps along the road.

00:014:57.000 --> 00:015:09.000
The firm believer will keep going, no matter what happens. Because what we're saying is worship God Alone. We are saying destroy all idols.

00:015:10.000 --> 00:015:14.000
And we are fanatically against building idols.

00:015:21.000 --> 00:015:31.000
This reminds me of... I don't know if it's a good joke. I mean, there's nothing bad about the language but...

